Contact Sheet: Panel 1 
\f4 \uc0\u8594 
\f0  Panel 2\
Use the attached contact sheet as the visual reference for the shot order and composition. Animate Panel 1 followed by Panel 2 as two distinct cinematic shots.\
A young Japanese couple in their mid-20s, wearing the same pale blue floral yukata and deep indigo-navy yukata shown in the reference, walk together through a traditional Japanese summer festival at blue hour.\
SHOT 1: The camera gently tracks behind and slightly beside the couple as they walk through a lantern-lit festival street. Festival visitors move naturally in the background. The woman notices a goldfish-scooping stall and turns her attention toward it. The man notices her interest and follows her gaze. Cut naturally to the stall.\
SHOT 2: The woman carefully attempts to scoop a goldfish from a shallow water basin using a fragile paper scoop. She slowly lifts it, but the wet paper tears and the fish slips back into the water. She freezes for a brief beat with a disappointed expression. The man tries to hold back a laugh, then smiles. She looks at him, and they share a small, spontaneous laugh.\
Use restrained human performances, natural hand movements, realistic water and paper behavior, warm practical lantern light, and subtle camera motion. Preserve the couple's facial appearance, hairstyles, clothing, and body proportions. The goldfish remain in the basin.\
End with the couple still standing beside the same goldfish stall, their shared laughter settling into a comfortable smile. This ending state must provide a coherent transition into the next clip.\
Cinematic realism, natural ambient festival sound, soft crowd chatter, footsteps, subtle water sounds, and the small sound of the paper scoop tearing. Gentle instrumental music may sit quietly underneath. No dialogue, no subtitles, no text overlays, no costume changes, no exaggerated comedy.\
