Use Panel 6 of the attached contact sheet as the ending composition reference. Create one continuous, quiet cinematic shot.\
The same Japanese couple remains at the same riverside location immediately after the fireworks display. They are still holding hands and wearing the same yukata. Seen from behind in a wide composition, they stand close together facing the dark river. The woman gently leans her head against the man's shoulder. He remains still and comfortable beside her.\
The last bright fireworks fade into a few distant sparks. Soft golden reflections ripple across the river and gradually diminish. The festival lanterns remain visible in the distance, providing continuity with the preceding scene.\
The camera slowly pulls back, revealing more of the quiet riverbank and the surrounding summer night. Keep the movement smooth and understated. Allow the final composition to settle without adding another major action.\
End with the couple still together, their joined hands visible, their silhouettes framed by the dark river and fading golden reflections. The emotional tone is warm, peaceful, and nostalgic.\
Cinematic realism, natural body contact, realistic fabric, subtle night ambience, distant crowd noise, and the fading reverberation of the final firework. Let the music soften and leave a brief natural ambience at the end. No dialogue, no subtitles, no text overlays, no new fireworks, no costume changes, no sudden scene change.\
